s for comparisons instead of symbols like `==` or `!=`. This avoids conflicts with the `>` redirection operator and keeps syntax unambiguous.\n\n## Comparison Operators\n\n| Operator | Meaning                  | Example               |\n|----------|--------------------------|-----------------------|\n| `-eq`    | Equal to                 | `5 -eq 5`   → `True`  |\n| `-ne`    | Not equal to             | `5 -ne 3`   → `True`  |\n| `-gt`    | Greater than             | `10 -gt 5`  → `True`  |\n| `-lt`    | Less than                | `3 -lt 7`   → `True`  |\n| `-ge`    | Greater than or equal    | `5 -ge 5`   → `True`  |\n| `-le`    | Less than or equal       | `4 -le 5`   → `True`  |\n\n> **Key Concept:** Comparison operators are **case-insensitive** by default. Add a `c` prefix for case-sensitive versions: `-ceq`, `-cne`, `-cgt`, etc.\n\n## String Operators: Wildcards and Regex\n\n**`-like`** uses wildcard patterns (`*` matches any characters, `?` matches one):\n\n```powershell\n\"PowerShell\" -like \"Power*\"     # True\n\"PowerShell\" -like \"P??er*\"     # True\n```\n\n**`-match`** uses **regular expressions** and populates the `$Matches` automatic variable:\n\n```powershell\n\"Error 404\" -match \"\\d+\"        # True\n$Matches[0]                      # 404\n```\n\n**`-replace`** performs regex-based substitution:\n\n```powershell\n\"2025-01-15\" -replace \"-\", \"/\"  # 2025/01/15\n\"Hello World\" -replace \"World\", \"PowerShell\"  # Hello PowerShell\n```\n\n## Logical Operators\n\nCombine conditions with logical operators:\n\n```powershell\n$age = 25\n($age -ge 18) -and ($age -lt 65)   # True\n($age -lt 13) -or ($age -gt 65)    # False\n-not ($age -eq 30)                  # True\n```\n\n> **Key Concept:** `-and` and `-or` use **short-circuit evaluation** — PowerShell stops evaluating as soon as the result is determined.\n\n## Arithmetic Operators\n\n```powershell\n10 + 3    # 13\n10 - 3    # 7\n10 * 3    # 30\n10 / 3    # 3.33333333333333\n10 % 3    # 1 (modulus — remainder)\n```\n\nPowerShell also supports `+=`, `-=`, `*=`, and `/=` shorthand:\n\n```powershell\n$count = 10\n$count += 5   # $count is now 15\n```\n0:{\"rsc\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"min-h-screen bg-zinc-950 text-zinc-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"header\",null,{\"className\":\"sticky top-0 z-10 border-b border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/80 backdrop-blur-xl\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto flex max-w-4xl items-center justify-between px-6 py-3.5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/fundamentals\",\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-zinc-500 transition-colors hover:text-zinc-300\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M10.5 19.5L3 12m0 0l7.5-7.5M3 12h18\"}]}],\"PowerShell Fundamentals\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/fundamentals/strings-arrays-hashtables\",\"className\":\"flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:border-zinc-700 hover:text-zinc-200\",\"title\":\"Strings, Arrays, and Hashtables\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M15.75 19.5L8.25 12l7.5-7.5\"}]}]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs tabular-nums text-zinc-500\",\"children\":[4,\" / \",9]}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/fundamentals/control-flow\",\"className\":\"flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:border-zinc-700 hover:text-zinc-200\",\"title\":\"Control Flow\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M8.25 4.5l7.5 7.5-7.5 7.5\"}]}]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 pb-4\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight\",\"children\":\"Operators and Comparisons\"}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{\"lesson\":{\"meta\":{\"title\":\"Operators and Comparisons\",\"description\":\"Comparison, logical, and arithmetic operators.\",\"slug\":\"operators-and-comparisons\",\"order\":4,\"prerequisites\":[\"m1-l3\"]},\"content\":\"$4\",\"exercises\":[{\"id\":\"m1-l4-ex1\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a comparison expression that checks if the variable $age is greater than or equal to 18.\",\"hints\":[\"Use the -ge operator for 'greater than or equal to'.\",\"PowerShell comparison operators start with a dash.\",\"Try: $age -ge 18\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\$age\\\\s+-ge\\\\s+18\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use $age -ge 18 to check if $age is greater than or equal to 18.\"}],\"solution\":\"$$age -ge 18\",\"explanation\":\"The -ge operator returns $true if the left operand is greater than or equal to the right operand.\"},{\"id\":\"m1-l4-ex2\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write an expression using -like to check if the variable $filename ends with \\\".ps1\\\" (use a wildcard pattern).\",\"hints\":[\"The -like operator uses wildcard patterns.\",\"The * wildcard matches any number of characters.\",\"Try: $filename -like \\\"*.ps1\\\"\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"-like\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use the -like operator for wildcard matching.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\$filename\\\\s+-like\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Compare $filename using -like.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"[\\\"']\\\\*\\\\.ps1[\\\"']\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use the wildcard pattern \\\"*.ps1\\\" to match files ending in .ps1.\"}],\"solution\":\"$$filename -like \\\"*.ps1\\\"\",\"explanation\":\"The -like operator uses wildcard patterns where * matches any number of characters. This checks if $filename ends with .ps1.\"},{\"id\":\"m1-l4-ex3\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Use -match with a regular expression to check if $email contains an @ symbol followed by at least one character, a dot, and more characters (basic email pattern).\",\"hints\":[\"The -match operator uses regular expressions.\",\"The @ symbol is literal in regex. Use \\\\. for a literal dot.\",\"Try: $email -match \\\"@.+\\\\..+\\\"\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"-match\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use the -match operator for regex matching.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\$email\\\\s+-match\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Compare $email using -match.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"@\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Your regex pattern should include @ to match the email format.\"}],\"solution\":\"$$email -match \\\"@.+\\\\..+\\\"\",\"explanation\":\"The -match operator tests the string against a regular expression. This pattern checks for @ followed by characters, a dot, and more characters — a basic email validation.\"},{\"id\":\"m1-l4-ex4\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write an expression using -replace to change all hyphens (-) to underscores (_) in the variable $filename.\",\"hints\":[\"The -replace operator takes a pattern and a replacement string.\",\"Syntax: $variable -replace 'find', 'replace'\",\"Try: $filename -replace \\\"-\\\", \\\"_\\\"\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"-replace\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use the -replace operator.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\$filename\\\\s+-replace\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Apply -replace to the $filename variable.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"-replace\\\\s+[\\\"']-[\\\"']\\\\s*,\\\\s*[\\\"']_[\\\"']\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Replace \\\"-\\\" with \\\"_\\\". Syntax: -replace \\\"-\\\", \\\"_\\\"\"}],\"solution\":\"$$filename -replace \\\"-\\\", \\\"_\\\"\",\"explanation\":\"The -replace operator uses regex to find matches and replaces them with the specified string. Here it swaps every hyphen for an underscore.\"},{\"id\":\"m1-l4-ex5\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a compound condition that checks if $temperature is greater than 0 AND less than 100. Use -and to combine the two comparisons.\",\"hints\":[\"Use -gt for greater than and -lt for less than.\",\"Combine two conditions with -and.\",\"Wrap each comparison in parentheses: ($temp -gt 0) -and ($temp -lt 100)\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"-and\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use the -and logical operator to combine conditions.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\$temperature\\\\s+-gt\\\\s+0\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Check that $temperature is greater than 0 using -gt.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\$temperature\\\\s+-lt\\\\s+100\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Check that $temperature is less than 100 using -lt.\"}],\"solution\":\"($temperature -gt 0) -and ($temperature -lt 100)\",\"explanation\":\"The -and operator returns $true only when both conditions are $true. Parentheses group each comparison for clarity and correct evaluation order.\"}],\"moduleSlug\":\"fundamentals\"}}],\"$L5\"]}],[\"$L6\"],\"$L7\"]}],\"isPartial\":false,\"staleTime\":300,\"varyParams\":null,\"buildId\":\"CCxR80sZRnjlIdOoXSFK7\"}\n5:[\"$\",\"footer\",null,{\"className\":\"border-t border-zinc-800/60\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto flex max-w-4xl items-center justify-between px-6 py-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/fundamentals/strings-arrays-hashtables\",\"className\":\"group flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:text-zinc-200\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4 transition-transform group-hov